 "id": "76dc9884c2a5",
 "task": "When should we schedule maintenance on the charging stations in the Bolzano area to minimise impact on users? Propose concrete weekday/time windows backed by observed usage.",
 "preset": "maintenance",
 "engine": "claude",
 "model": "sonnet",
 "status": "ok",
 "started_at": "2026-11-14T06:39:15.250252+00:00",
 "markdown": "## Answer\nSchedule Bolzano-area maintenance in the early morning, with Thu 05:00-07:00 as the first choice (occupancy 0.066 over 5 comparable dates) [E2]. Tue 05:00-07:00 (0.124) and Fri 05:00-07:00 (0.146) are the fallbacks [E2]. The busiest site, BZ_C_RISPARMIO_01, has no comparably quiet window and needs separate scheduling [E4].\n\n## Key findings\n- Bolzano-wide occupancy over the 56-day window was 0.435 [E2].\n- The three lowest-usage 2-hour windows are Thu 05:00-07:00 (0.066, 5 dates), Tue 05:00-07:00 (0.124, 4 dates) and Fri 05:00-07:00 (0.146, 4 dates) [E2].\n- The busiest windows to avoid are Wed 20:00-22:00 (0.72), Sat 21:00-23:00 (0.654) and Mon 20:00-22:00 (0.651) [E2].\n- The 06:00 hour is 0.08 on Thu, 0.161 on Tue and 0.227 on Fri, and usage climbs from 08:00, so work should finish by 07:00 [E2].\n- Weekend nights are not safe: Sat is 0.821 at 02:00 and 0.491 at 04:00 in the Bolzano-wide grid [E2].\n- BZ_C_RISPARMIO_01 (2 points) has occupancy 0.669, full_time 0.462 and 203 observed starts [E3]. Its lowest windows are Sat 19:00-21:00 (0.449), Mon 15:00-17:00 (0.465) and Fri 13:00-15:00 (0.469) [E4].\n- BZ_BOEHLER_01 has a single point that was fully occupied 0.57 of the time, so any outage there removes all capacity [E3].\n\n## Recommendation\n- Default slot: Thu 05:00-07:00, then Tue 05:00-07:00, then Fri 05:00-07:00 [E2].\n- BZ_C_RISPARMIO_01: schedule separately, with Mon 15:00-17:00 as the first option and Fri 13:00-15:00 as the second [E4]. Usage there stays high in these windows, so consider doing the work one point at a time.\n- Do not schedule in the Wed, Sat or Mon evening peaks, or on Saturday nights [E2].\n- Confirm with a repeat check once more weeks of data are available.\n\n## Limitations & unknowns\n- Occupancy reflects status only, not energy, sessions, demand or faults [E1].\n- The early-morning windows rest on 4 to 5 comparable dates [E2]. In the Bolzano-wide grid, 44 cells fall below the 4-date minimum [E2], and several 00:00-05:00 cells are null (no observable data) [E2].\n- Only 43 of 51 sites had data in the window [E1]. 22 sites were excluded from the ranking for under 24 hours of exposure [E3].\n- Coverage for the top five ranked sites ranges from 0.033 to 0.227, which is low [E3]. BZ_C_RISPARMIO_01 has coverage of 0.147 [E3]. All 65 of its grid cells fall below the minimum date count [E4].\n- Data-quality and stale flags were not checked, so that information is unavailable.\n- Bolzano is defined by a bounding box, not the municipal boundary [E1].\n\n## Sources\n- [E1] dataset_overview — Open Data Hub South Tyrol EChargingPlug status, window 2026-09-19..2026-11-14\n- [E2] hourly_profile(scope=bolzano) — Open Data Hub South Tyrol EChargingPlug status, window 2026-09-19..2026-11-14\n- [E3] rank_sites(metric=occupancy) — Open Data Hub South Tyrol EChargingPlug status, window 2026-09-19..2026-11-14\n- [E4] hourly_profile(scope=Neogy-AMPECO:78226) — Open Data Hub South Tyrol EChargingPlug status, window 2026-09-19..2026-11-14",
